  "2026-08-10T23:01:02.643Z","harness:codex","Completion evidence 2026-08-11: shipped a persisted SDK-first measurement registry with item, dependency-kind, graph, validate, health, history, links, provider, and derived arithmetic sources; strict declaration validation, cycle/non-numeric/divide-by-zero failures, and per-evaluation cost receipts with caller ceilings. Focused linked tests passed, packed CLI manual acceptance persisted and queried a real measurement in an isolated project, and the repo-wide release pipeline reached exact 100/100/100/100 coverage with 7,201 passing tests."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T23:01:03.175Z","harness:codex","Measurement affordability is part of the data contract: built-in and contributed adapters must return cost with value, while derived measurements aggregate child cost and fail cycles or invalid arithmetic explicitly."
